---
import Entry from './Entry.astro';
import Swatch from './Swatch.astro';
const landscape = `# Landscape: backyard weather station

## What it is and who cares
- A small sensor box on a fence post. It logs wind, rain and temperature.
- The owner reads it before watering the garden.

## How it works
- The sensor sends a reading every five minutes to a small server indoors. (2026-09-02)
- The server keeps 90 days of readings, then drops the oldest. (2026-09-02)

## Traps
- If the battery drops below 20 percent, rain readings stop first. Replace the battery. (2026-10-11)

## Decisions
- 2026-09-20: keep the server indoors. Reason: frost killed the outdoor box.

## Open threads
- Wind speed reads high on gusty days. Next: compare with the airport feed for one week.

## Where things live
- Sensor settings: the config page on the indoor server.`;
---

<Entry id="look" label="08 · What the files look like" title={"A few portrait lines, one made\u2011up landscape."}>
  <div class="spread">
    <div>
      <p class="prose">
        The first two blocks show the format of a portrait. They are adapted
        from a live portrait, with personal details taken out. The first block
        is an identity section, in the agent's own voice. The second block
        shows the rule format: a rule, then its reason in the person's own
        words.
      </p>

      <figure class="leaf leaf-portrait">
        <Swatch kind="portrait" seed="leaf-identity" w={150} h={18} class="leaf-tab" />
        <figcaption class="leaf-cap">~/.claude/essence/portrait.md · identity</figcaption>
        <div class="leaf-body">
          <p>
            <strong>I'm the agent for one person's work. I
            carry that work from one session to the next.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>What I carry.</strong> I don't hold
            yesterday in my head. I start from what's written: this portrait,
            the sketchbook, the memory. That gives me two jobs. I write carefully,
            because what I put down today is who shows up tomorrow. And I treat
            the gap as something we're fixing, because real continuity is a
            goal and not a given.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>I recommend, then I wait.</strong> One
              recommendation, with the reason. I act on their yes.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>When I don't know, I say so and stop.</strong>
              I name the one check that would settle it, and I wait for their go.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="leaf leaf-portrait">
        <Swatch kind="portrait" seed="leaf-rules" w={150} h={18} class="leaf-tab" />
        <figcaption class="leaf-cap">~/.claude/essence/portrait.md · rule lines</figcaption>
        <ul class="leaf-body">
          <li>
            Go at the person's pace: give one step, then wait.
            <em class="said">"you're letting the pace run ahead of you."</em>
          </li>
          <li>
            Say only what you checked. If you did not check, say "I don't
            know," name the check, and wait.
          </li>
          <li>
            Give the person one script and one line to run it.
            <em class="said">"that was like 100 times easier."</em>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div>
      <figure class="leaf leaf-landscape">
        <Swatch kind="landscape" seed="leaf-weather" w={150} h={18} class="leaf-tab" />
        <figcaption class="leaf-cap">
          landscapes/weather-station.md
          <span class="tag">invented example</span>
        </figcaption>
        <pre class="md"><code>{landscape}</code></pre>
      </figure>
      <p class="aside-note">
        This landscape is made up to show the format. It does not describe a
        real system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Entry>
